Make config.h.W32 accurate for MSVC/clang-cl.

Upstream's `src/config.h.W32` was calibrated for MinGW-GCC and TinyCC;
two of its guards leave MSVC/clang-cl in an inconsistent state that
happens to compile against older UCRT SDKs but breaks against modern
ones (Windows 10 SDK >= 10.0.20000):

  1. `HAVE_UMASK 1` is restricted to `__MINGW32__ || __TINYC__`. That was
     accurate when MSVC's `<io.h>` only exposed `_umask`, but modern UCRT
     (`<corecrt_io.h>`) declares POSIX-compat `_ACRTIMP int umask(int)`.
     With HAVE_UMASK left undefined, `src/makeint.h`/`src/misc.c` fall
     back to `extern mode_t umask(mode_t)` + a stub definition — the
     linkage mismatch against UCRT's `dllimport` decl then fails with
     `error C2375: 'umask': redefinition; different linkage`.

  2. Once HAVE_UMASK is set for MSVC, the `typedef int mode_t` tucked
     inside the same guarded block in `src/makeint.h` no longer fires.
     MinGW's `<sys/types.h>` supplies `mode_t`, but MSVC's does not, so
     unrelated call sites like `src/misc.c:685` (`mode_t mask;` in
     `get_tmpfd`) then fail with `error C2065: 'mode_t': undeclared
     identifier`. Add `#define mode_t int` for `_MSC_VER` (which covers
     clang-cl too), matching the shape upstream uses for `gid_t`/`uid_t`
     immediately below.

The sibling HAVE_STRCASECMP / HAVE_STRNCASECMP guards are intentionally
left alone: MSVC ships `_stricmp` / `_strnicmp` (already surfaced via
HAVE_STRCMPI / HAVE_STRICMP / ... elsewhere in the file), not the POSIX
spellings, so widening those would set a false positive.

diff --git a/src/config.h.W32 b/src/config.h.W32
--- a/src/config.h.W32
+++ b/src/config.h.W32
@@ -415,7 +415,7 @@
 #define HAVE_UINTMAX_T 1

 /* Define to 1 if you have the `umask' function. */
-#if defined(__MINGW32__) || defined(__TINYC__)
+#if defined(__MINGW32__) || defined(__TINYC__) || defined(_MSC_VER)
 # define HAVE_UMASK 1
 #endif

@@ -563,6 +563,11 @@
 /* Define to 'int' if <sys/types.h> doesn't define. */
 #define gid_t int

+/* MSVC and clang-cl don't declare `mode_t` in <sys/types.h>; MinGW does. */
+#ifdef _MSC_VER
+#define mode_t int
+#endif
+
 /* Define to 'int' if <sys/types.h> does not define. */
 /* GCC 4.x reportedly defines pid_t.  */
 #ifndef _PID_T_
